  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>A and D cannot be oxidised by bromine water as they do not have hemiacetal linkage. The acid hydrolysis of A leads to a laevorotatory solution. A is sucrose which is dextrorotatory, on acid hydrolysis gives mixture of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math>-D-glucopyranose&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math>-D-fructofuranose, the mixture is laevorotatory.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/b6af0d57-7aef-49e9-b668-a1279ac3b853.png\" style=\"width: 952px; height: 249px;\" /></p></blockquote>",
